+// NINE (neither-inclusive-nor-exclusive) set-associative L2 TLB - FIXED.
+//
+// Bugs found in tlb.cc.nine.sa / tlb.hh.nine.sa and fixed here:
+//   1. l2_remove(va) matched L2 entries by VA only, ignoring the PCID/ASN
+//      that is folded into the stored key. demapPage() on one address space
+//      could therefore invalidate a different address space's L2 translation
+//      for the same VA (and leave the demapped process's own stale L2 copy
+//      behind if that copy had a different PCID encoding at the time it was
+//      looked up). Fixed: l2_remove(va, asn) builds the same concAddrPcid()
+//      key used at insert time and matches on that exact key.
+//   2. serialize()/unserialize() only covered the L1 array. A checkpoint
+//      restore silently dropped all L2 state, so a restored run has fewer
+//      cached translations than an uninterrupted run would (not a crash, but
+//      an observable, undocumented behavior change and a lost-state bug for
+//      any policy study that checkpoints). Fixed: L2 valid bits + entries
+//      are serialized/restored alongside L1.
+//   3. No stat distinguished an L2 hit/promotion from an L1 hit, so a dead L2
+//      (e.g. because of bug 1's corruption) was not visible in stats.txt.
+//      Fixed: added l2Hits/l2Insertions/l2Evictions.
+//   4. L2 geometry (128 sets x 4 ways), index hash, replacement policy and
+//      insert-on-L2-hit behavior were compile-time constants, which blocked
+//      the requested runtime sweep. Fixed: all four are environment-selected
+//      in the constructor (see tlb.hh.nine.fixed top comment for the names);
+//      one gem5.opt binary covers every variant.
+//
+// Not changed (shared with stock/other lanes, out of this lane's scope):
+//   PCID is still folded into the low 12 address bits (concAddrPcid); this
+//   works because PCID is <=12 bits and vpn here is always page-aligned, but
+//   it is still a fragile representation vs. a real tagged-TLB ASID field.
+
 #include "arch/x86/tlb.hh"
 
